  "description": "OPANIF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H110 Co6 Dy4 N6 O37,9(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.038-3.779 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.69-106.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4Co6(L)4(HL)2(OAc)6(OCH2CH2OH)2(HOCH2CH2OH)(H2O)]·9CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
